1
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:08,137
Good evening, I'm Anders Fjell, and this is Nordic Crypto.

2
00:00:08,137 --> 00:00:13,908
Issue number four, with the Nordic crypto news from the 19th
to the 25th of October, 2026.

3
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:18,985
Tonight: Norway's minister says crypto mining in data
centres is not widespread.

4
00:00:18,985 --> 00:00:21,620
Sweden's central bank looks at an e-krona.

5
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,474
And Apple and BlackRock in the bitcoin headlines.

6
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:32,629
Norway's digitalisation minister, Torgeir Micaelsen, told
the Storting in a written answer that crypto mining in data

7
00:00:32,629 --> 00:00:33,953
centres is not widespread.

8
00:00:33,953 --> 00:00:37,860
The register shows mining at eight of 113 data centres.

9
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:42,099
The government is assessing a temporary, limited ban,
subject to EEA law.

10
00:00:42,099 --> 00:00:44,078
Ságat reported the answer.

11
00:00:44,666 --> 00:00:50,592
TV 2 reports that five people are on trial in Oslo District
Court over a home robbery in which the robbers demanded two

12
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:51,887
million dollars in crypto.

13
00:00:51,887 --> 00:00:53,949
One posed as a food courier.

14
00:00:53,949 --> 00:00:56,866
The five are charged, and have not been convicted.

15
00:00:59,078 --> 00:01:05,081
In Sweden, Riksbank deputy governor Per Jansson told Reuters
that Sweden should prepare for a possible e-krona, pointing

16
00:01:05,081 --> 00:01:06,882
to the digital euro and stablecoins.

17
00:01:06,882 --> 00:01:08,893
No decision has been taken.

18
00:01:08,893 --> 00:01:10,934
Hurbra reported the interview.

19
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:17,395
Dagens Nyheter reports on criticism after Israel's prime
minister Benjamin Netanyahu suggested crypto could help get

20
00:01:17,395 --> 00:01:18,709
around possible sanctions.

21
00:01:18,709 --> 00:01:22,688
The Bank of Israel replied that cryptocurrencies cannot
serve that purpose.

22
00:01:23,286 --> 00:01:28,560
Realtid reports that Apple has asked a US court to dismiss a
lawsuit from three investors who say they lost one point

23
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,851
eight million dollars through a fake bitcoin wallet app in
the App Store.

24
00:01:31,851 --> 00:01:35,559
Apple says it cannot be held responsible for outside
fraudsters.

25
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:43,782
And BlackRock has filed for a bitcoin fund designed to limit
losses, ticker P-BIT, Kryptovalutaguiden reports.

26
00:01:43,782 --> 00:01:48,074
The filing is incomplete, and the shares may not be sold
until it becomes effective.

27
00:01:48,686 --> 00:01:54,679
Finally, the Bitcoin Ordinals art project Tiny Vikings
planned to unveil what it calls the world's largest Tiny

